      <title>Time-lapse RESOLFT nanoscopy empowered by deep learning</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78580-z</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 11 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78580-z"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-78580-z&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;The authors use two deep-learning methods for RESOLFT nanoscopy: HDN denoising enables five-fold longer live-cell imaging, while spatial upsampling with temporal context restores subsampled data for fourfold higher frame rates and reduced artifacts.</content:encoded>
