    <item>
      <title>Intensification of near-inertial currents in the Atlantic Ocean over the past two decades</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78555-0</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 11 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78555-0"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-78555-0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Ocean drifter observations reveal that Atlantic near-inertial currents intensified by almost 4% per decade during 2003–2022. This intensification is primarily driven by changes in wind forcing associated with mesoscale weather systems.</content:encoded>
