    <item>
      <title>HCV incidence and prevalence trends among people who use drugs in France 2004 to 2023</title>
      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78598-3</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 11 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78598-3"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-78598-3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Authors show in 2013-2023 France saw a substantial reduction in hepatitis C virus prevalence and incidence among people who use drugs. Widespread treatment and harm reduction drove the decline, bringing France closer to WHO 2030 elimination targets.</content:encoded>
