      <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78648-w</link>
      <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature Communications, Published online: 11 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-78648-w"&gt;doi:10.1038/s41467-026-78648-w&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Existing approaches for biosynthetic gene cluster (BGC) discovery are labor-intensive, depend on de novo DNA synthesis and are difficult to scale. Here we show that an automated platform for one-step assembly and refactoring of BGCs facilitates facile novel product discovery.</content:encoded>
      <dc:title>An automated operon refactoring workflow for heterologous expression of non-ribosomal peptide biosynthetic gene clusters</dc:title>
